            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0948" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.679 Residence and Establishment/11:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-18T13:00:00+02:00">March 18, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—11:25 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>19. Department’s 15, March 17, 6 p.m. On March 21 I am going to Ankara for a week
                    or so, and I shall be guided by circumstances with regard to the use of the very
                    helpful authorization and instructions which are contained in paragraphs (1) to
                    (3). Probably it will be desirable to do so with a view to reassuring the Turks
                    concerning the sincerity of American intentions respecting the negotiation
                    eventually of a brief treaty of residence and establishment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
